---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base>
  <header>
    <div class="container">
      <h1>FIFA World Cup 2026</h1>
      <div class="subtitle">🧠 12 Shocking Facts That'll Blow Your Mind</div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="container">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="hero-card">
        <div class="hero-overlay"></div>
        <img src="/images/stadium.jpg" alt="Stadium" class="hero-img" />
        <div class="hero-content">
          <h2 class="hero-title">World Cup Trivia<br />You Won't Believe</h2>
          <p class="hero-sub">Shocking. Funny. Mind-blowing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="trivia-grid">

        <div class="trivia-card" style="--accent-color: #f59e0b">
          <div class="trivia-img">
            <img src="/images/trivia/flags_north_america.jpg" alt="Flags of USA, Mexico and Canada" />
            <span class="trivia-img-license">CC BY-SA 4.0 — Isa8a, Wikimedia Commons</span>
          </div>
          <div class="trivia-number">01</div>
          <h3 class="trivia-title">Bigger Than Ever</h3>
          <p class="trivia-text"><span class="emoji-inline">🌍</span> The 2026 World Cup is the <strong>biggest in history</strong>: 48 teams, 3 host nations, 104 matches across 39 days. That's a 50% expansion from the 32-team format used since 1998. More teams, more chaos, more drama.</p>
          <div class="trivia-tag">2026</div>
        </div>

        <div class="trivia-card" style="--accent-color: #f59e0b">
          <div class="trivia-img">
            <img src="/images/trivia/trophy.jpg" alt="FIFA World Cup Trophy at FIFA World Museum, Zürich" />
            <span class="trivia-img-license">CC BY-SA 4.0 — Ank Kumar, Wikimedia Commons</span>
          </div>
          <div class="trivia-number">02</div>
          <h3 class="trivia-title">The Trophy Was Stolen</h3>
          <p class="trivia-text"><span class="emoji-inline">🐶</span> In 1966, the <strong>Jules Rimet Trophy</strong> was stolen from a London exhibition. A week later, a dog named <strong>Pickles</strong> found it wrapped in newspaper under a bush. The trophy was saved, and Pickles became a national hero.</p>
          <div class="trivia-tag">History</div>
        </div>

        <div class="trivia-card" style="--accent-color: #3b82f6">
          <div class="trivia-img">
            <img src="/images/trivia/curacao_beach.jpg" alt="Curaçao island beach" />
            <span class="trivia-img-license">CC0 Public Domain — Martijn Meijerink, Skitterphoto</span>
          </div>
          <div class="trivia-number">03</div>
          <h3 class="trivia-title">David vs Goliath</h3>
          <p class="trivia-text"><span class="emoji-inline">🇨🇼</span> <strong>Curaçao</strong> (pop. ~156,000) is the smallest nation ever to qualify for a men's World Cup. The United States has ~330 million people. That's roughly <strong>2,115 Curaçaos</strong> inside one USA.</p>
          <div class="trivia-tag">2026</div>
        </div>

        <div class="trivia-card" style="--accent-color: #ef4444">
          <div class="trivia-img">
            <img src="/images/trivia/suarez.jpg" alt="Luis Suárez playing for Uruguay at the 2014 World Cup" />
            <span class="trivia-img-license">CC BY-SA 2.0 — Jimmy Baikovicius</span>
          </div>
          <div class="trivia-number">04</div>
          <h3 class="trivia-title">Bite #3</h3>
          <p class="trivia-text"><span class="emoji-inline">🦷</span> At the 2014 World Cup, <strong>Luis Suárez</strong> bit Italian defender Giorgio Chiellini on the shoulder. This was the <strong>third time</strong> he bit an opponent on a pitch. He got a 4-month ban. Yes, third time. Some people never learn.</p>
          <div class="trivia-tag">History</div>
        </div>

        <div class="trivia-card" style="--accent-color: #22c55e">
          <div class="trivia-img">
            <img src="/images/trivia/bmo_field.jpg" alt="BMO Field soccer stadium, Toronto" />
            <span class="trivia-img-license">Pexels License — Harrison Haines</span>
          </div>
          <div class="trivia-number">05</div>
          <h3 class="trivia-title">Canada's Homecoming</h3>
          <p class="trivia-text"><span class="emoji-inline">🍁</span> Canada is playing its first World Cup <strong>on home soil</strong>. Their only previous appearance? <strong>1986</strong> — a 40-year gap. They lost all 3 group matches back then without scoring a single goal. This time will be different.</p>
          <div class="trivia-tag">2026</div>
        </div>

        <div class="trivia-card" style="--accent-color: #22c55e">
          <div class="trivia-img">
            <img src="/images/trivia/sugarloaf.jpg" alt="Sugarloaf Mountain at sunrise, Rio de Janeiro" />
            <span class="trivia-img-license">CC BY-SA 4.0 — Donatas Dabravolskas, Wikimedia Commons</span>
          </div>
          <div class="trivia-number">06</div>
          <h3 class="trivia-title">Iron Streak</h3>
          <p class="trivia-text"><span class="emoji-inline">🇧🇷</span> <strong>Brazil</strong> is the only nation to have played in <strong>all 22 World Cups</strong> since 1930. Not Germany, not Argentina, not Italy — only Brazil. They've won 5, but showing up every single time for 96 years is a trophy in itself.</p>
          <div class="trivia-tag">History</div>
        </div>

        <div class="trivia-card" style="--accent-color: #ef4444">
          <div class="trivia-img">
            <img src="/images/trivia/trionda_ball.jpg" alt="Adidas Trionda — 2026 World Cup official match ball" />
            <span class="trivia-img-license">CC BY-SA 4.0 — OhanaUnited, Wikimedia Commons</span>
          </div>
          <div class="trivia-number">07</div>
          <h3 class="trivia-title">The 4-Panel Secret</h3>
          <p class="trivia-text"><span class="emoji-inline">⚽</span> The official 2026 match ball — <strong>Adidas Trionda</strong> — has only <strong>4 stitched panels</strong>, the fewest of any World Cup ball ever. Fewer seams means less drag, more swerve, and unpredictable flight at high-altitude stadiums like Mexico City.</p>
          <div class="trivia-tag">2026</div>
        </div>

        <div class="trivia-card" style="--accent-color: #3b82f6">
          <div class="trivia-img">
            <img src="/images/trivia/maracana.jpg" alt="Estádio do Maracanã in Rio de Janeiro" />
            <span class="trivia-img-license">CC BY-SA 4.0 — Boaventuravinicius, Wikimedia Commons</span>
          </div>
          <div class="trivia-number">08</div>
          <h3 class="trivia-title">Maracanã's Millions</h3>
          <p class="trivia-text"><span class="emoji-inline">🏟️</span> The 1950 World Cup final between Uruguay and Brazil packed an estimated <strong>199,854 spectators</strong> into Maracanã — the largest crowd ever for a football match. Still the record, 76 years later.</p>
          <div class="trivia-tag">History</div>
        </div>

        <div class="trivia-card" style="--accent-color: #3b82f6">
          <div class="trivia-img">
            <img src="/images/trivia/airplane.jpg" alt="Airplane flying above clouds" />
            <span class="trivia-img-license">Pexels License — Pixabay</span>
          </div>
          <div class="trivia-number">09</div>
          <h3 class="trivia-title">Globe Trotters</h3>
          <p class="trivia-text"><span class="emoji-inline">✈️</span> The 2026 World Cup spans <strong>3 countries</strong> across North America. A team could play Vancouver → Mexico City → Miami — a journey of over <strong>8,000 miles</strong>. Never have players clocked more air miles in a single tournament.</p>
          <div class="trivia-tag">2026</div>
        </div>

        <div class="trivia-card" style="--accent-color: #3b82f6">
          <div class="trivia-img">
            <img src="/images/trivia/referee_yellow_card.jpg" alt="Referee holding a yellow card during a match" />
            <span class="trivia-img-license">Unsplash License — Bob Oh</span>
          </div>
          <div class="trivia-number">10</div>
          <h3 class="trivia-title">The Ref's Nightmare</h3>
          <p class="trivia-text"><span class="emoji-inline">🟨</span> Portugal vs Netherlands, 2006: the referee handed out <strong>16 yellow cards and 4 red cards</strong> — the most cards ever shown in a single World Cup match. 20 cards total. The ref probably needed a massage after that one.</p>
          <div class="trivia-tag">History</div>
        </div>

        <div class="trivia-card" style="--accent-color: #a855f7">
          <div class="trivia-img">
            <img src="/images/trivia/italy_flag_photo.jpg" alt="Flag of Italy against blue sky" />
            <span class="trivia-img-license">CC0 Public Domain — Petr Kratochvil</span>
          </div>
          <div class="trivia-number">11</div>
          <h3 class="trivia-title">The Fall of Giants</h3>
          <p class="trivia-text"><span class="emoji-inline">🇮🇹</span> <strong>Italy</strong> — 4-time World Champion, runner-up in 1994 and 2000 — failed to qualify for the <strong>third consecutive</strong> World Cup. They lost to Bosnia and Herzegovina on penalties. A football superpower watching from home. Again.</p>
          <div class="trivia-tag">2026</div>
        </div>

        <div class="trivia-card" style="--accent-color: #a855f7">
          <div class="trivia-img">
            <img src="/images/trivia/octopus.jpg" alt="Octopus underwater" />
            <span class="trivia-img-license">Pexels License — pspov</span>
          </div>
          <div class="trivia-number">12</div>
          <h3 class="trivia-title">Octopus Oracle</h3>
          <p class="trivia-text"><span class="emoji-inline">🐙</span> <strong>Paul the Octopus</strong> predicted 8/8 World Cup matches correctly in 2010, including the final between Spain and the Netherlands. He lived in an aquarium in Germany and chose his predictions by eating from labeled boxes. An octopus was never wrong.</p>
          <div class="trivia-tag">History</div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" style="text-align:center;padding: 40px 0">
      <p style="color:var(--textDim);font-size:0.85rem">
        Facts collected from FIFA archives and football history records.
        <br />Hero photo by <a href="https://www.pexels.com" style="color:var(--accent2)" target="_blank">Pexels</a> (CC0). Card images public domain / Pexels — see each image.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .hero-card {
    position: relative;
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    min-height: 320px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .hero-img {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .hero-overlay {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(10,14,23,0.92), rgba(20,27,45,0.7));
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .hero-content {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 40px 20px;
  }
  .hero-title {
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent2), var(--gold));
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
    background-clip: text;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .hero-sub {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--textDim);
  }

  .trivia-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(380px, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .trivia-card {
    position: relative;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 24px;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .trivia-card::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 4px;
    background: var(--accent-color);
    border-radius: 14px 14px 0 0;
  }
  .trivia-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    border-color: var(--accent-color);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-color) 20%, transparent);
  }

  .trivia-img {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    height: 180px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    background: var(--surface2);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .trivia-img img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .trivia-img img[src$=".svg"],
  .trivia-img img[src*="trophy.jpg"] {
    object-fit: contain;
    padding: 20px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-color) 8%, var(--surface));
  }
  .trivia-img .trivia-img-license {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    background: rgba(0,0,0,0.7);
    color: #aaa;
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    padding: 3px 8px;
    text-align: center;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
  }
  .trivia-number {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-color) 30%, var(--surface2));
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .emoji-inline {
    font-size: 1.1em;
    margin-right: 2px;
  }
  .trivia-title {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-color);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .trivia-text {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--textDim);
  }
  .trivia-text strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .trivia-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-color);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-color) 15%, transparent);
    padding: 2px 10px;
    border-radius: 10px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .hero-title { font-size: 1.5rem; }
    .trivia-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .trivia-card { padding: 16px; }
  }
</style>
